            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that New York\u2019s proper\u2011cause licensing requirement violates the Second Amendment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "050f4a002f60f97729bd9a1da879cf1dc0c08955859b56aac8966c0a4bb3e76f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-050f4a002f60-0008-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 80,
              "start": 80
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh, joined by the Chief Justice, concurred, emphasizing that the Second Amendment guarantees the right to self\u2011defense and that New York\u2019s regime is inconsistent with that right."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "050f4a002f60f97729bd9a1da879cf1dc0c08955859b56aac8966c0a4bb3e76f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-050f4a002f60-0008-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 82,
              "start": 82
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Barrett concurred, noting that the right is not unlimited and that prohibitions on dangerous and unusual weapons are historically permissible."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "050f4a002f60f97729bd9a1da879cf1dc0c08955859b56aac8966c0a4bb3e76f",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-050f4a002f60-0008-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 87,
